This entry supersedes both the original completion claim above and the first correction
entry. It is written after the owner rejected an intermediate "complete" claim a second time
(that claim had redefined C-001..C-014 as Prisma-model-existence checks instead of the actual
workflow criteria in PHASE-1-SPECIFICATION.md, and used design-inspection language in place of
executed evidence for the Phase 2 report). This entry reports only what was actually executed
in this final pass, against the ORIGINAL, unredefined criteria.

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
EXECUTED (real, re-runnable, evidence pasted in the reports/journal below)
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

1. 42 real per-rule kernel test cases (14 rules x POS/NEG/MISSING), executed against the
   actual MaiKernel.evaluateCondition() evaluator — not grammar-shape validation. Found and
   fixed a real production bug in the process: composite operators (all/any/not) were dead
   code because the evaluator gated them on a field the approved rule grammar never sets.
   File: src/services/__tests__/MaiKernel.rules.test.ts (43/43 passing).

2. Service test suites for CurriculumCompiler, DualApprovalGate, EmergencyContentManager,
   TraceabilityGraph, plus 5 more services built this pass (EvidenceIngestion,
   CausalStatusService, InterventionClosureService, ManifestGuard, ContentSupersessionService,
   KernelSelfAudit, HonestDashboardBuilder, AiAssist) — all against the real seeded SQLite
   database, no mocks.

3. The ORIGINAL C-001..C-014 from PHASE-1-SPECIFICATION.md section 3 re-verified as
   running-code workflows: file ingestion with a real 5-state quarantine machine and SHA-256
   hashing (C-001), confidentiality-gated AI routing with a real audit trail (C-002), both AI
   and manual atom authoring paths (C-003), human-only causal-status promotion with a real
   transition graph (C-004), publication gate rejecting DRAFT atoms (C-005), baseline-only
   compilation (C-007), deterministic compilation with a REAL bug found and fixed — the hash
   was previously insensitive to actual content (C-008), automatic effectiveness-based closure
   (C-009, partial — no per-atom completion table exists), forward/reverse traceability
   (C-010), content recall with a REAL bug found and fixed — the recall query was an
   unconditional stub returning an empty array (C-011), and frozen-manifest immutability via a
   real SQLite trigger with two explicitly documented limitations (C-013). Full report:
   PHASE-1-VERIFICATION-REPORT-v2.md.

4. All 6 Phase 2 governance gates executed for real, no design-inspection language anywhere in
   the report: dual approval (5/5 tests), emergency auto-expiry using a real 31-day backdated
   timestamp — no mocked clocks (7/7 tests, 1 REAL bug found and fixed — isExpired() never
   checked time at all), supersession + disposition records (3/3 tests), kernel self-audit
   that actually calls the kernel — REAL bug found and fixed: it previously never called the
   kernel and fabricated 100%-pass results unconditionally (4/4 tests), honest dashboards — 3
   REAL bugs found and fixed in one file: cross-intervention data leakage, a silently-wrong
   unverified count, and a status comparison that could never be true against real data
   (4/4 tests), and immutability re-run. Full report: PHASE-2-VERIFICATION-REPORT-v2.md.

5. Ownership/licensing embed: LICENSE (proprietary, Conform-Edge Quality Consulting LLC),
   NOTICE (software vs. embedded course-content IP boundary), copyright headers in all 69
   .ts/.tsx source files with a check script wired into prebuild — proven for real to fail
   the build when a header is missing (deliberately stripped one, confirmed the build failed
   naming the exact file, restored it), package.json author/license fields, and a version and
   copyright stamp in the UI footer (every page) and in the enrollments export, reports
   export, and the parked Defense Dossier prototype's output contract.

6. A ninth and tenth real defect found and fixed while finishing this pass: AiAssist's audit
   logging always threw a foreign-key violation and silently never persisted (2 call sites);
   AiAssist read the wrong evidence field (a citation label, not the actual document text) for
   both the LLM prompt and source-span extraction. And an eleventh: intermittent test failures
   traced to SQLite concurrent-writer contention across Jest's parallel workers, fixed by
   forcing serial execution (chosen over an in-memory test DB specifically to keep the C-013
   trigger in the test path).

TOTAL REAL DEFECTS FOUND AND FIXED THIS PASS: 11. All 11 were found only by writing and
executing real tests against real data — none were visible to code review, the type checker,
or the "18 tests passed" grammar-only test that the very first pass relied on.

