───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DEFERRED / NOT IMPLEMENTED (named explicitly, not silently dropped)
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

- C-012 (Defense Dossier PDF export): NOT IMPLEMENTED. A real scope conflict exists between
  PHASE-1-SPECIFICATION.md (lists it as an exit criterion) and the original
  AUTONOMOUS-RUN-DIRECTIVE.md (explicitly lists "Defense Dossier build-out" as out of scope).
  Logged in OPEN-QUESTIONS.md Q-001 with a recommendation, not silently resolved either way.
  The existing prototype (_prototypes/DefenseDossierBuilder.ts) does not compile against the
  current schema and was not rebuilt in this pass — only its output contract was updated with
  the version-stamp requirement, for whenever it is properly rebuilt.

- C-006 classification inheritance: PARTIAL. Atom status/approval progression is real and
  verified; automatic inheritance of classification from source evidence is not implemented
  anywhere in the codebase (confirmed by code search) — every atom in every test has its
  classification set explicitly by the caller. Logged in OPEN-QUESTIONS.md Q-002.

- C-009 per-atom completion tracking: PARTIAL. Assignment-level status transitions,
  supervisor observation, effectiveness evidence, and automatic closure are all real and
  verified. No table or service exists for per-atom completion/gating (the spec's "Ready for
  Assessment button appears after Atom-003" behavior) — the schema has this for the legacy
  Course/Lesson model but not for LearningAtom. Logged in OPEN-QUESTIONS.md Q-004.

- C-013 trigger scope: documented limitation, not fixed. The real SQLite immutability
  trigger only protects rows with status ACTIVE; a SUPERSEDED manifest is not protected
  (proven by a negative-control test, not assumed). Not widened in this pass without explicit
  owner sign-off, per the directive's caution against unilaterally touching governance-relevant
  DB objects. Logged in OPEN-QUESTIONS.md Q-003.

- C-013 error-text specificity: documented driver limitation, not fixable in this pass.
  Prisma's SQLite connector maps the trigger's custom RAISE(ABORT, message) to a generic P2003
  error and does not surface the literal string the spec names. The block itself is real and
  verified; the exact error text is not, for reasons outside this codebase's control on SQLite.

- Full UI for the Phase 1 workflow: NOT BUILT. All C-001..C-014 evidence in this pass comes
  from direct service-layer execution against the real database, not from a browser UI —
  because no such UI exists (the empty API route directories under src/app/api/hf/ were never
  populated with route.ts files, in this pass or any prior one). This is the real, only
  application code path for this behavior currently; not a shortcut taken to avoid building UI.

- Adversarial/concurrent-load testing of the Phase 2 gates: NOT ATTEMPTED. The 121 tests
  are unit/integration tests against direct service calls. Concurrent-approval races, load
  testing the manifest trigger under simultaneous writers, and similar adversarial scenarios
  were not tested and are not claimed to have been.

- Phase 3 work: NOT STARTED, per original directive scope (unchanged from the first pass).

